window.ADG_IDX=[{"s":"Welcome","p":"Congratulations!","u":"welcome.html#congratulations","k":"welcome, congratulations, Wedding Team","t":"Thank you for choosing us to celebrate your wedding. The whole Auberge des Gallant team is delighted to be part of it. This site brings together everything you will need for your preparations: the main milestones, our deadlines, our policies, our tools and our favourite suppliers. Come back to it as often as you like, it is here to make your life easier. We look forward to celebrating with you! The Auberge des Gallant Wedding Team"},{"s":"Welcome","p":"How to use this site","u":"welcome.html#how-to-use-this-board","k":"how to use, navigation, ◆ symbol","t":"Each section covers one topic. To find information quickly: Timeline: your key dates with the Auberge, then your preparations period by period, from 18 months before until the day after the wedding. It also comes as an Excel spreadsheet: enter your wedding date and you will know exactly when to plan each step. Topic sections: reception halls, decor, menu, guests, accommodations, suppliers and the wedding day. Downloadable tools: timeline, budget, floor plans, place cards and other templates. In the timeline, the ◆ symbol marks a step you complete with the Auberge."},{"s":"Welcome","p":"A few key terms","u":"welcome.html#a-few-key-terms","k":"glossary, terms, wedding coordinator, banquet manager, trusted person, wedding planning service","t":"Some words you will see throughout this site: Your wedding coordinator: your contact at the Auberge before the big day. She plans with you everything related to our spaces and services. Your banquet manager: on site on the wedding day from 2 p.m., she makes sure the reception runs smoothly and on schedule in our spaces. Your trusted person: someone close to you whom you appoint to coordinate your day outside of our services. Wedding planning service: a professional wedding planning service, independent from the Auberge, that you can hire to coordinate your day."},{"s":"Welcome","p":"Well supported, every step of the way","u":"welcome.html#well-supported-every-step-of-the-way","k":"commitment, wedding coordinator, banquet manager, trusted person, planning, roles, responsibilities","t":"A successful wedding relies on careful preparation and clearly defined roles. At the Auberge, our team takes care of everything related to our facilities and services, so that every detail of your reception is ready. Before the big day: your wedding coordinator She plans with you everything related to our spaces and services: layout, menu, reception schedule and logistics. Everything is ready before you arrive. On the wedding day: your banquet manager On site from 2 p.m., she is your contact person at the Auberge. She makes sure the reception runs smoothly and follows the planned schedule in our spaces. Our advice: your trusted person Entrust the coordination of your day to someone close who knows your wishes well, or to a professional wedding planning service. That way, you can fully enjoy every moment."},{"s":"Welcome","p":"What your trusted person looks after","u":"welcome.html#what-your-trusted-person-looks-after","k":"","t":"The Auberge does not offer a wedding planning service or overall coordination of the day. The following items are therefore handled by your trusted person or by the wedding planning service you hire: Travel and transportation Liaising with your outside suppliers Preparations at the church or elsewhere The photo schedule Transitions outside our facilities Unexpected situations and guests' questions While your loved ones look after your day, we look after your reception."},{"s":"Welcome","p":"Checklist: what stays in your hands","u":"welcome.html#checklist-what-stays-in-your-hands","k":"checklist, not included, to plan, trusted person, suppliers, officiant, decor, transportation","t":"Our team takes care of everything related to our spaces, our table and our service. This checklist covers the items handled by you or by the person you appoint, so nothing is forgotten. As soon as you book Appoint your trusted person or hire a wedding planning service Choose your officiant and review the legal requirements for marriage with them Book your suppliers: photographer, videographer, DJ or musicians, florist, cake maker, hair and makeup Plan the sound system and microphone for your ceremony and your evening (often provided by your DJ) Tell your guests about accommodation options at the Auberge (check-in from 4 p.m., no later than 6 p.m.) In the months before Order your wedding cake (we serve it, à la carte) Choose your personal decor: centrepieces, signage, guest book, place cards Plan your personal flowers: bouquets, boutonnieres and floral decor for the hall Arrange transportation for your guests, if needed Plan preparations at the church or another location, if applicable A few weeks before Confirm your guest list, menu choices and allergies Tell us how many suppliers will be having the meal Prepare your floor plan Send your wedding coordinator your suppliers' contact details and arrival times Give your trusted person the schedule of the day and the list of key contacts Set the photo schedule Plan to set up your decor from 8 a.m. on the wedding day Gifts for guest rooms, if any: bring them to us ready and wrapped, ideally the day before (no later than 9:30 a.m. on the day) Would you like to set up your decor the day before? It is sometimes possible, depending on our events calendar. We can confirm it during the week before your wedding. On the wedding day: what your trusted person handles Set up your personal decor from 8 a.m., or supervise the setup Set out the place cards and any additions to the table setting (menus, small gifts, table decor) Welcome your outside suppliers and answer their questions Handle travel and transitions outside the Auberge Answer your guests' questions Handle unexpected situations outside our facilities The day after Pick up your personal belongings no later than 7:30 a.m. (we will have stored them for you) Pick up your decor and your suppliers' items If you rent the Pavillon without a package Hire your caterer Obtain your liquor permit and arrange your bar service"},{"s":"Welcome","p":"Contact us","u":"welcome.html#contact-us","k":"contact, Audrey, phone, email, appointment, visit, address","t":"Audrey Loiselle Wedding Sales and Events Coordinator 450-459-4241, ext. 312 mariage@gallant.qc.ca In the office Tuesday to Saturday. Meetings and visits are by appointment, Tuesday to Saturday, between 10 a.m. and 3 p.m. Send us a few options and we will confirm the time that works. Auberge des Gallant, 1171, chemin Saint-Henri, Sainte-Marthe (Québec) J0P 1W0 www.gallant.ca To make communication easier, please always include your full wedding date in the subject line of your emails."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"8 to 12 months before","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#8-to-12-months-before","k":"wedding coordinator, wedding party, officiant, style, florist, attire","t":"Meeting with your wedding coordinator: menu, layout, accommodations and reception schedule."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"6 to 8 months before","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#6-to-8-months-before","k":"menu, menu tasting, cake, decor, transportation, Save the date","t":"Menu and bar planning with your wedding coordinator. Wedding menu tasting: by appointment, to taste our menu and finalize your choices."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"1 month before","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#1-month-before","k":"final count, meal choices, Grande Finale, final meeting, final payment, floor plan","t":"Final guest count and meal choices. The kitchen needs them to order food. \"La Grande Finale\" form to send to mariage@gallant.qc.ca: allergies and dietary restrictions, suppliers' contact details and arrival times, confirmation or changes to rooms. Final meeting: held within the 30 days before the wedding. Final payment: made at the final meeting, by cheque or bank transfer. Credit cards are not accepted for amounts over $3,000. Complete floor plan, to hand in 4 weeks before the wedding, at the final meeting: table layout, number of guests per table, number of each dish per table, seating of guests with allergies and table numbers. Also list the extra tables you need (gifts, cards, candy bar or other). Outside food to be reheated: submit your request no later than 3 weeks before. It must be approved by the chef and your wedding coordinator, and fees apply."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"3 weeks before","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#3-weeks-before","k":"vows, speeches, photos, fitting","t":"Place cards: prepare them following our guide, with each guest's meal choice and allergy symbols."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"From day 21 to day 14 before","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#from-day-21-to-day-14-before","k":"","t":"In case of cancellations, small reductions can still be made to your count."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"2 weeks before","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#2-weeks-before","k":"decor, tablecloths, flow, 14 days","t":"Decor items to bring to the Auberge: tablecloths, table runners, napkins, chair covers and anything needed to set up the hall. From 14 days before the wedding, no substitutions or changes can be made to the final count or meal choices, and no credit is given."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"72 hours before","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#72-hours-before","k":"","t":"The floor plan is considered final. Small, reasonable changes are still possible but not guaranteed, and changing the plan may result in fees."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"The day before, ideally","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#the-day-before-ideally","k":"","t":"Gifts for your guests' rooms (if any): bring them to us ready and wrapped, ideally the day before. Drop-off is no earlier than 3 days before the wedding and no later than 9:30 a.m. on the day. We then place them in the rooms. Fees may apply."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"The wedding day","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#the-wedding-day","k":"wedding day, 8 a.m. access, rings, hair, makeup","t":"Access to your reception hall from 8 a.m. for decorating and setup. Cake and flowers delivered on the day, or as arranged in advance with your wedding coordinator. Place cards set on the tables by you or your trusted person, before guests enter the hall. Our team does not handle this."},{"s":"Key dates with the Auberge","p":"The day after","u":"key-dates-with-the-auberge.html#the-day-after","k":"","t":"Pick-up of your personal belongings no later than 7:30 a.m. Just like you the day before, the next couple has access to the hall from 8 a.m. Open bar tab (if any) to be settled before you leave."},{"s":"Timeline","p":"Is your wedding less than 12 months away?","u":"timeline.html#is-your-wedding-less-than-12-months-away","k":"less than 12 months, short timeline, priorities, late booking","t":"No need to worry: a wedding can be planned very well in under a year. Here are the essentials, in order of priority. Then pick up the timeline at the period you have reached. Right now Sign your contract and meet your wedding coordinator: menu, layout, accommodations and reception schedule Book the most in-demand suppliers first: photographer, DJ or musicians, officiant Appoint your trusted person or hire a wedding planning service Set your budget and your guest list Within the next month Choose your wedding attire: making and alteration times are often long Book your florist, your cake maker and your stylists (hair, makeup) Send your invitations, or a \"Save the date\" card if invitations are still a while away Send your guests the booking link for your room block Book your wedding menu tasting (by appointment, at least 1 week ahead) Then Follow the timeline from the period you have reached. Steps whose date has already passed should be done right away: the Excel timeline flags them automatically. Deadlines with the Auberge stay the same no matter when you booked: final count 1 month before, final meeting within the 30 days before the wedding, no changes from 14 days before."},{"s":"Timeline","p":"12 to 18 months before","u":"timeline.html#12-to-18-months-before","k":"budget, contract, date, photographer, DJ, insurance","t":"Set your budget (template in \"Downloadable tools\") Draw up a preliminary guest list Choose your date, book your reception hall and ceremony site, sign your contract Book the photographer, videographer and DJ or musicians Consider wedding insurance to protect your deposits: check with your current insurer, who usually offers optional coverage Think about who will coordinate your day: a trusted person or a professional wedding planning service"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"8 to 12 months before","u":"timeline.html#8-to-12-months-before","k":"wedding coordinator, wedding party, officiant, style, florist, attire","t":"Meet your wedding coordinator: menu, layout, guest accommodations, reception schedule Choose your wedding party Choose and meet your officiant (religious or legal aspects) Define your style: colours, mood, vision Choose your florist Choose your wedding attire Book your other suppliers (see our favourite suppliers) Create your planning binder and meet with your parents to discuss it Optional: gift registry, engagement party Start dreaming about your honeymoon"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"6 to 8 months before","u":"timeline.html#6-to-8-months-before","k":"menu, menu tasting, cake, decor, transportation, Save the date","t":"Plan the menu and bar service with your wedding coordinator Book your wedding menu tasting (by appointment, at least 1 week ahead) Optional: send your \"Save the date\" cards, with accommodation details Taste and choose your cake with your cake maker Plan the decor and design of your reception Discuss bouquets with your florist and the flowers available on your date Book transportation for the day Confirm your suppliers with written contracts, to avoid misunderstandings Check your stylists' availability (hair, makeup) and travel Optional: engagement photo shoot, rehearsal dinner planning"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"4 to 6 months before","u":"timeline.html#4-to-6-months-before","k":"invitations, stationery, attire, ceremony, wedding night","t":"Order invitations and stationery Finalize your wedding attire and accessories Plan the ceremony in detail with your officiant Book your wedding night room (included in Le Gallant and Le Gastronomique packages) Optional: bachelor or bachelorette party Room block: send your guests the booking link as soon as you receive it (sent within the 6 months before the wedding)"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"2 to 4 months before","u":"timeline.html#2-to-4-months-before","k":"wines, floor plan, invitations, rings, alterations, favours, vows","t":"Review your menu and wine choices with your wedding coordinator Prepare a preliminary floor plan (your hall's plan in \"Downloadable tools\") Finalize the guest list and addresses Send the invitations (about 3 months before), asking for a reply at least 6 weeks before the wedding Order the cake Order your printing and personalized decor items, if any Shop for your wedding rings Finalize the wedding party's outfits, alterations and tuxedos Book dress alteration appointments (10 to 12 weeks before) Book your stylists and do your hair and makeup trials Finalize contracts and rentals with your suppliers, then do a first confirmation Order or make your wedding favours (we offer maple syrup favours) Buy gifts for your parents and wedding party Start writing your vows and choosing your readings Passport, visas and vaccines for the honeymoon; finalize the trip"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"6 to 9 weeks before","u":"timeline.html#6-to-9-weeks-before","k":"RSVPs, meal choices, Grande Finale, room block, documents, officiant","t":"Keep a tracking list of RSVPs and meal choices Start filling out the \"La Grande Finale\" form Confirm the last details with your suppliers Confirm the rooms in your block: rooms not booked are released automatically 4 weeks before the wedding Check with your officiant which documents are required for the marriage and, if applicable, for a name change"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"1 month before","u":"timeline.html#1-month-before","k":"final count, meal choices, Grande Finale, final meeting, final payment, floor plan","t":"Send the final guest count and meal choices Send the \"La Grande Finale\" form to mariage@gallant.qc.ca Hold your final meeting (within the 30 days before the wedding) and make the final payment Confirm the schedules of all your suppliers Hand in the complete floor plan at the final meeting (4 weeks before): tables, guests and dishes per table, guests with allergies, numbers"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"3 weeks before","u":"timeline.html#3-weeks-before","k":"vows, speeches, photos, fitting","t":"Finalize your vows, readings, song list and speech list Prepare the shot list for your photographer or videographer Confirm the flow of the day and where the wedding party will get ready Have the final dress fitting, with all accessories Buy the guest book, create the guest program, write your speech Confirm transportation and welcome for out-of-town guests Prepare the list of your suppliers and their contact details Optional: book your massage therapy treatments at Spa Gallant with your wedding coordinator, no later than the final meeting"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"2 weeks before","u":"timeline.html#2-weeks-before","k":"decor, tablecloths, flow, 14 days","t":"Bring all the decor items needed for setup to the Auberge Finalize the flow of the reception with your wedding party, your suppliers and the Auberge Start packing for your honeymoon From now on, the final count and meal choices can no longer be changed."},{"s":"Timeline","p":"1 week before","u":"timeline.html#1-week-before","k":"place cards, room gifts, suppliers, tips, access the day before","t":"Prepare your place cards and finalize your floor plan Send the Auberge any last useful information Drop off your gifts for the rooms, ready and wrapped, ideally the day before (no later than 9:30 a.m. on the day, no earlier than 3 days before) Access to the hall the day before: possible depending on our events calendar, confirmed only during the week before the wedding Confirm details and arrangements with your suppliers Prepare tip envelopes, if applicable Brief your trusted person: schedule, suppliers, unexpected situations Choose who will bring the important items (cake knife, toasting glasses, guest book) Optional: last beauty treatments A manicure for the groom, if he wishes"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"The final days","u":"timeline.html#the-final-days","k":"day before, rehearsal, supplier payments, Spa, relaxation","t":"3 days before Have the dress steamed, pick up the suit Set the order of the wedding party for the ceremony entrance and exit The day before Put the suppliers' final payments in envelopes Gather all the decorations and items for the day Give the required documents to your officiant Ceremony rehearsal, if applicable Optional: rehearsal dinner, massage therapy at Spa Gallant If you love tradition, gather something old, something new, something borrowed and something blue Confirm the honeymoon details Take a moment to relax with your loved ones, then get a good night's sleep"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"The wedding day","u":"timeline.html#the-wedding-day","k":"wedding day, 8 a.m. access, rings, hair, makeup","t":"Access to your reception hall from 8 a.m. for decorating Introduce your trusted person to your banquet manager Give the rings to the best man or maid of honour Exchange your gifts and give your parents' and wedding party's gifts Hair and makeup; allow at least two hours to get dressed Take time to eat (lunch in your room available by pre-order) Breathe, let go and enjoy every moment"},{"s":"Timeline","p":"After the wedding","u":"timeline.html#after-the-wedding","k":"day after, personal belongings, thank-you cards, photos, returns","t":"Pick up your belongings at the Auberge the next day, no later than 7:30 a.m. Return rented and borrowed items; have the dress cleaned Write and mail your thank-you cards Complete your gift registry, exchanges and returns Choose your photos with your photographer Enjoy your new life as newlyweds"},{"s":"Our reception halls and the ceremony","p":"Phoenix Hall","u":"our-reception-halls-and-the-ceremony.html#phoenix-hall","k":"Phoenix, capacity, 200 guests, tent, dimensions","t":"Grand and contemporary. Large windows onto the forest, cathedral ceiling, private terrace with a tent, large dance floor and bar. Capacity: up to 200 guests Private cocktail space: Phoenix tent Hall dimensions: 60 x 40 feet Reception until 3 a.m. possible, with additional fees"},{"s":"Our reception halls and the ceremony","p":"Vaudreuil-Soulanges Hall","u":"our-reception-halls-and-the-ceremony.html#vaudreuil-soulanges-hall","k":"Vaudreuil-Soulanges, capacity, 80 guests, gazebo, fireplace","t":"Elegant and warm. Bright, with a fireplace and private terrace, it suits weddings where closeness matters most. Capacity: 35 to 80 guests Private cocktail space: outdoor gazebo Hall dimensions: 30 x 40 feet Reception ends at 1 a.m. (no extension, as the hall is close to the guest rooms)"},{"s":"Our reception halls and the ceremony","p":"Le Cellier","u":"our-reception-halls-and-the-ceremony.html#le-cellier","k":"Cellier, small wedding, 60 guests, wine cellar, gazebo","t":"Cosy and refined. Nestled beside our wine cellar, it offers an intimate setting for smaller weddings. Capacity: 60 guests or fewer Private cocktail space: outdoor gazebo Hall dimensions: 27 x 30 feet Reception ends at 1 a.m. (no extension, as the hall is close to the guest rooms)"},{"s":"Our reception halls and the ceremony","p":"Pavillon des Gallant","u":"our-reception-halls-and-the-ceremony.html#pavillon-des-gallant","k":"Pavillon, maple grove, 125 guests, tent, two fireplaces","t":"Rustic, exclusive and countryside. Set apart from the main site, surrounded by a maple grove, with a cathedral roof, large windows and two fireplaces. Capacity: 80 to 125 guests Private cocktail space: Pavillon tent Hall dimensions: 50 x 30 feet Reception until 3 a.m. possible, with additional fees"},{"s":"Our reception halls and the ceremony","p":"The ceremony in our gardens or under the pergola","u":"our-reception-halls-and-the-ceremony.html#the-ceremony-in-our-gardens-or-under-the-pergola","k":"ceremony, gardens, pergola, willows, chairs, signing table","t":"Under the willows in our gardens or under the Pavillon pergola, our team prepares the space and takes care of the cleanup. Included with your ceremony Chair setup for your guests Signing table with tablecloth Welcome table with fresh water and glassware Natural and potted flowers A table for the DJ and an easel, free of charge on request Need extra tables? Let your wedding coordinator know in advance. Ceremony music and sound, the officiant and personalized decor are provided by your suppliers."},{"s":"Our reception halls and the ceremony","p":"Rain or power outage: our backup plans","u":"our-reception-halls-and-the-ceremony.html#rain-or-power-outage-our-backup-plans","k":"rain, backup plan, bad weather, power outage, electricity, generators","t":"If it rains Each reception hall has a backup plan prepared in advance, for both the ceremony and the cocktail. After the ceremony, our service team is stationed at key points to direct your guests to the cocktail. In case of a power outage The Auberge is equipped with generators. If the power goes out, they take over so your reception can carry on."},{"s":"Our reception halls and the ceremony","p":"Useful dimensions for your decor","u":"our-reception-halls-and-the-ceremony.html#useful-dimensions-for-your-decor","k":"dimensions, tables, tablecloths, table runners, dance floor, aisle, head table","t":"Auberge Oval table: 4 x 8 ft Rectangular table: 2.5 x 8 ft Head table: 4 x 6 ft White tablecloth: 86 x 132 in; black tablecloth: 90 x 156 in Table runner: 12 ft long Ceremony gazebo: 9.8 ft wide, 3.75 ft front Ceremony aisle: 4 x 40 ft Phoenix Hall Wallpaper wall: 10 x 15 ft (draped) Dance floor: 15 x 35 ft (head table included) Tent: 40 x 60 ft Pavillon des Gallant Rectangular table: 2.5 x 7.5 ft Head table: 4 x 6 ft White tablecloth: 86 x 132 in; black tablecloth: 90 x 156 in Table runner: 12 ft long Dance floor: 12 x 50 ft Ceremony pergola: 10 x 10 ft, 7 ft high Patio under the pergola: 11 x 13 ft Tent: 20 x 60 ft"},{"s":"Hall, setup and decor","p":"Included with your package","u":"hall-setup-and-decor.html#included-with-your-package","k":"included, Chiavari chairs, tablecloths, charger plates, glassware, setup","t":"Cocktail space Tables dressed in white or black linens (low and cocktail tables), chairs Reception hall Tables dressed in white or black linens White Chiavari chairs with cushions Table runners, from our 23 colours Gold charger plates, cutlery and glassware White cloth napkins After the reception Teardown and regular cleaning Storage of your belongings for easy pick-up the next morning"},{"s":"Hall, setup and decor","p":"Access to your reception hall","u":"hall-setup-and-decor.html#access-to-your-reception-hall","k":"access, 8 a.m., day before, schedule, end of evening, extension, 1 a.m., 3 a.m., suppliers","t":"On the wedding day: from 8 a.m., for decorating and setup. Earlier or the day before: possible depending on our events calendar. The answer is confirmed only during the week before the wedding. End of the reception: your contract includes use of the hall until 1 a.m., at no charge. Extension until 3 a.m.: available only in Phoenix Hall and the Pavillon des Gallant, at $450 per hour, plus taxes and service charges. It can be requested in advance or on the night. The bar option (cash bar, open tab or extended open bar) is to be arranged with your wedding coordinator. Suppliers: they leave the hall no later than 1 hour after the end of the evening."},{"s":"Hall, setup and decor","p":"The bar after 1 a.m.","u":"hall-setup-and-decor.html#the-bar-after-1-a-m","k":"bar, 1 a.m., cash bar, open tab, running bill","t":"If you extend the evening and would like to keep the bar open after 1 a.m., there are two options: Cash bar: each guest pays for their own drinks. Open tab: you cover your guests' drinks. Only the couple can authorize it, and the amount is settled before you leave the next morning."},{"s":"Hall, setup and decor","p":"Our table runners","u":"hall-setup-and-decor.html#our-table-runners","k":"table runners, colours, palette, satin, etamine, ivory, white, champagne, silver, charcoal grey, black, damask, coffee brown, dusty rose, blush pink, candy pink, coral, terracotta, burgundy, eggplant, chocolate brown, lilac, purple, dusty blue, sapphire blue, royal blue, olive green, forest green","t":"Your table runners are included with your package. Choose from our 23 colours, in satin, crushed satin or crushed etamine. They are 12 feet long and 6 or 12 inches wide depending on the model. Let your wedding coordinator know your choice when planning your reception."},{"s":"Hall, setup and decor","p":"Your tablecloths, table runners and chair covers","u":"hall-setup-and-decor.html#your-tablecloths-table-runners-and-chair-covers","k":"tablecloths, table runners, chair covers, napkins, 14 days, delivery","t":"You may supply your own tablecloths, table runners, napkins or chair covers. Bring them to the Auberge at least 14 days before the wedding: our setup team needs them to prepare the hall. Fees apply if items arrive late. Our team sets up your tablecloths, table runners, cloth napkins and charger plates at no charge, since they replace ours. For chair covers, additional setup fees may apply. Your place cards, and any other addition to the table setting provided by the Auberge (menus, small gifts, table decor, etc.), are set out by you or your trusted person. Our team does not handle this."},{"s":"Hall, setup and decor","p":"Decor: what is not permitted","u":"hall-setup-and-decor.html#decor-what-is-not-permitted","k":"policies, confetti, sparklers, smoke, fireworks, not permitted","t":"For everyone's safety and out of respect for the premises, the following are not permitted indoors: Confetti, popcorn, feathers or anything else that requires major cleanup Sparklers and smoke machines (even water-based) Fireworks, unless approved by the Municipality of Sainte-Marthe and the owners Failure to follow these guidelines may result in additional fees."},{"s":"Hall, setup and decor","p":"Candles","u":"hall-setup-and-decor.html#candles","k":"candles, votives, candle holders, flame, diagram","t":"No wax candles or votives directly on the tables. They must be in a candle holder or vase, and the flame must be covered: the holder rises above the wick by at least one third of its height. Have your candle holders approved by your wedding coordinator before buying them: she can also suggest alternatives."},{"s":"Hall, setup and decor","p":"After the reception","u":"hall-setup-and-decor.html#after-the-reception","k":"day after, personal belongings, pick-up, 7:30 a.m.","t":"At the end of the evening, our team gathers your items on one table or in one room. Pick them up the next morning, no later than 7:30 a.m.: just like you the day before, the next couple has access to the hall from 8 a.m. After that time, the Auberge is no longer responsible for breakage or theft, unless storage fees are paid."},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"Our packages at a glance","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#our-packages-at-a-glance","k":"packages, Classique, Gallant, Gastronomique, courses, wine","t":"Le Classique 1.5-hour cocktail (sangria or punch, alcohol-free option, 4 canapés per person), 3-course menu, ½ bottle of wine per person, coffee and tea. Le Gallant 1.5-hour cocktail, 4-course menu, ½ bottle of wine per person, 4-hour open bar in the evening, the couple's night in a King or double Queen room, and breakfast. Le Gastronomique Open bar during the cocktail, sparkling wine toast, 5-course menu, ½ bottle of wine per person, 4-hour open bar in the evening, the couple's night and breakfast. Your package details are set out in your contract."},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"Your main course choices","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#your-main-course-choices","k":"main course, meal choice, supplement, children","t":"Each package includes three main course choices: two from the menu and one vegetarian option. Additional meal choice: $5 per person, per choice Some dishes carry a supplement depending on the package (filet mignon, lamb shank, etc.) Children's menus available: penne with rosé or tomato sauce, or homemade chicken fingers and fries"},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"Vegetarians, allergies and dietary restrictions","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#vegetarians-allergies-and-dietary-restrictions","k":"vegetarian, vegan, allergies, gluten-free, lactose, dietary restrictions","t":"All our packages offer a vegetarian or vegan option. In that case, every course, from starter to dessert, is vegetarian. We can also accommodate dietary restrictions: gluten-free, lactose-free, shellfish and others. List them in the \"La Grande Finale\" form."},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"The wedding menu tasting","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#the-wedding-menu-tasting","k":"tasting, menu tasting, dinner, menu, wines","t":"Before finalizing your choices, come taste our wedding menu, our wines and our service, and make your choices with confidence. By appointment Book your tasting with your wedding coordinator at least 1 week in advance. Lunch: Thursday, Friday and Saturday Dinner: Thursday and Friday Fees apply Ideal timing: 6 to 8 months before the wedding"},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"Our Wedding Show and its Tasting Dinner","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#our-wedding-show-and-its-tasting-dinner","k":"Wedding Show, Tasting Dinner, suppliers, January, event","t":"Every year, we open our doors to couples-to-be: some twenty of our favourite suppliers, from every field, gathered under one roof at the Auberge. Admission is free. The Tasting Dinner At the end of the show, Phoenix Hall becomes a wedding reception for a Tasting Dinner: a chance to experience a wedding at the Auberge just as your guests will. Limited seating, reservation required Fees apply Next edition Wedding Show: Saturday, January 16, 2027, from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. Tasting Dinner: from 4 p.m., $75 per person, plus taxes and service Ask your wedding coordinator about upcoming dates."},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"The open bar","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#the-open-bar","k":"open bar, shooters, premium drinks","t":"Shooters and doubles are not included in any package. Would you like specific or premium drinks? Let your wedding coordinator know in advance. No bottles are placed on the tables: guests do not serve themselves."},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"Alcohol: what our permit requires","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#alcohol-what-our-permit-requires","k":"alcohol, permit, bring your own wine, tailgating, gifts","t":"Under our liquor permit, it is strictly forbidden to bring in and consume alcohol not purchased on site, including in the parking lots, common areas, gardens and tents. Bottles of alcohol cannot be given to guests as gifts. Tailgating is prohibited; a fine may apply for misconduct or damage. All special orders must go through the Auberge, under certain conditions; additional fees apply."},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"Outside food","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#outside-food","k":"outside food, reheating, 3 weeks","t":"It is possible, as long as it is ready to serve: we do not handle food that is not prepared in our kitchens. If food needs to be reheated, the chef and your wedding coordinator must approve it at least 3 weeks in advance, and fees apply."},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"Your wedding cake","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#your-wedding-cake","k":"cake, cutting, delivery, dessert, 45 minutes","t":"Delivered on the day, or as arranged in advance with your wedding coordinator. To serve the cake as dessert, take the cake-cutting photos before the main course is served: plating takes about 45 minutes. Cake cutting and service: free if it replaces our dessert; otherwise, $2.50. Send your serving instructions to your wedding coordinator."},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"The late-night buffet","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#the-late-night-buffet","k":"buffet, late night, poutine, pizza, platters","t":"For one last treat: platters (cheese, charcuterie, sandwiches, mignardises, macarons, pizza), bar-style stations (nachos, ice cream) or individual portions (poutine, smoked meat). Base fee of $350, plus a per-person cost based on your selection."},{"s":"Menu, bar and tasting","p":"Lunch while you get ready","u":"menu-bar-and-tasting.html#lunch-while-you-get-ready","k":"lunch, room, sandwiches, getting ready, pre-order","t":"Getting ready at the Auberge? We can serve platters of assorted sandwiches and crudités in your room. Pre-order required, options to discuss with your wedding coordinator."},{"s":"Guests, floor plan and place cards","p":"Final count and meal choices","u":"guests-floor-plan-and-place-cards.html#final-count-and-meal-choices","k":"final count, guests, meal choices, cancellations, 14 days","t":"1 month before: final guest count and meal choices. From day 21 to day 14: small reductions are possible in case of cancellations. 14 days before: no more substitutions or changes, and no credit. Tip: ask your guests to reply at least 6 weeks before the wedding, with their meal choice and allergies."},{"s":"Guests, floor plan and place cards","p":"Your floor plan","u":"guests-floor-plan-and-place-cards.html#your-floor-plan","k":"floor plan, tables, numbers, 72 hours, final meeting","t":"To hand in 4 weeks before the wedding, at the final meeting: the table layout the number of guests per table the number of each dish, per table the seating of guests with allergies the table numbers any extra tables you need (gifts, cards, candy bar or other) The hall is set up only once. Small last-minute changes are accommodated where possible, but nothing is guaranteed within 72 hours of the wedding, and fees may apply. Floor plans of our reception halls"},{"s":"Guests, floor plan and place cards","p":"Place cards are required","u":"guests-floor-plan-and-place-cards.html#place-cards-are-required","k":"place cards, name, meal choice, allergies, tables","t":"Place cards allow our team to serve each guest without hesitation and to handle allergies safely. Each one shows: the guest's name their main course choice (beef, chicken, salmon, vegetarian, etc.) the symbol or symbols for their allergies or dietary restrictions, if any Set them directly on the tables, at each guest's seat, before guests enter the hall, not on a welcome table. You or your trusted person set them out: our team does not handle this. Having them printed? Send our guide to your printer."},{"s":"Guests, floor plan and place cards","p":"Creating your place cards","u":"guests-floor-plan-and-place-cards.html#creating-your-place-cards","k":"place cards, format, tent card, font, size, colours, icon","t":"Recommended format Folded tent card, 3.5 x 2 in or 4 x 2.5 in, readable from both sides of the table Single-sided printing is possible, but double-sided is preferred Main course choice In words or with an icon. The icon is then solid black, so it is not confused with the allergy and dietary restriction symbols, which are in colour. Typography Guest name: minimum 18 pt, ideally 22 to 32 pt Meal choice: minimum 12 pt, ideally 14 to 16 pt An elegant but easy-to-read font Colours Light background (white, ivory, cream, very pale pastel) and dark text Our guide shows good examples and examples to avoid. Your wedding coordinator may also ask to approve your design. Place card guide (PDF)"},{"s":"Guests, floor plan and place cards","p":"Allergy and dietary restriction symbols","u":"guests-floor-plan-and-place-cards.html#allergy-and-dietary-restriction-symbols","k":"symbols, icons, allergies, dietary restrictions, vegetarian, vegan, gluten","t":"Place the applicable symbols right next to each guest's main course choice. Vegetarian · Vegan · Peanuts and tree nuts · Gluten · Shellfish and crustaceans · Eggs · Lactose · Soy · Sulphites · Fish · Other allergy or restriction (to specify) Each symbol is at least 1.25 cm (0.5 in) Its proportions and colours are not altered It is visible at a glance To avoid Codes or abbreviations alone (B, P, VG, etc.) Symbols smaller than the minimum size Low-contrast colours Symbols placed far from the meal choice In our template, if you choose the \"Other allergy or restriction\" symbol, a box appears where you can type the details. Keep it short (e.g., Mango, Passion fruit, Halal). Place card templates and symbols (ZIP)"},{"s":"Guests, floor plan and place cards","p":"Guest book, program and speeches","u":"guests-floor-plan-and-place-cards.html#guest-book-program-and-speeches","k":"guest book, program, speeches, cake knife","t":"Think about these about 3 weeks before: the guest book, the guest program and the toast speech. Also appoint someone to bring the important items to the reception, such as the cake knife or toasting glasses."},{"s":"Accommodations","p":"Staying at the Auberge","u":"accommodations.html#staying-at-the-auberge","k":"rooms, accommodations, breakfast, thermal baths, pool, pets, charging stations, Tesla","t":"Give your guests the comfort of staying on site after the celebration. 42 rooms, King with sofa bed or double Queen Wi-Fi, smart TV, balcony or terrace, air conditioning, electric fireplace, Nespresso machine, bathrobes and towels In the morning: breakfast, access to the thermal baths and heated outdoor pool 4 rooms adapted for people with reduced mobility (Kéroul member) Some rooms welcome pets (conditions apply) 4 electric vehicle charging stations on site, including 1 Tesla charger"},{"s":"Accommodations","p":"Your room block","u":"accommodations.html#your-room-block","k":"room block, preferred rate, booking link, guests, $279, additional guest, child, release 4 weeks","t":"With each of our reception halls, a block of rooms is guaranteed for your guests: Phoenix Hall: 15 rooms Pavillon des Gallant: 10 rooms Vaudreuil-Soulanges Hall: 6 rooms Le Cellier: 4 rooms The booking link A booking link will be sent to you within the 6 months before your wedding date. Share it with your guests: it gives them access to the preferred rate. Only bookings made through this link receive that rate. The rooms in your block are held for your guests until 4 weeks before the wedding. Rooms not booked by then are released automatically. The preferred rate $279 per night in 2027 and $289 in 2028, double occupancy, breakfast included Up to 2 additional guests per room: ask your wedding coordinator about the current applicable fees Adding a child to the room: $15 Access to our wellness facilities the next morning Taxes extra. Would your guests rather stay elsewhere? There are hotels nearby: you will find their contact details in the \"Nearby lodging and transportation\" sheet, further down this page."},{"s":"Accommodations","p":"The wedding night","u":"accommodations.html#the-wedding-night","k":"wedding night, couple's room, overnight stay","t":"The Le Gallant and Le Gastronomique packages include one night in a King or double Queen room (double occupancy) and breakfast for the couple. With Le Classique, book your room through your wedding coordinator."},{"s":"Accommodations","p":"On the wedding day, in your room","u":"accommodations.html#on-the-wedding-day-in-your-room","k":"room, getting ready, check-in, 1 p.m., 4 p.m., bathrobes","t":"Couple's room: available from 1 p.m. at the latest. Guest rooms: check-in from 4 p.m. Your guests can also check in during the first minutes of the cocktail, until 6 p.m. at the latest. Before the ceremony, the bride waits in her room until the wedding coordinator comes to get her. Our team makes sure most guests are present before she makes her entrance. Bathrobes are not permitted in the Auberge's common areas."},{"s":"Accommodations","p":"Nearby lodging and transportation","u":"accommodations.html#nearby-lodging-and-transportation","k":"hotels, Rigaud, Vaudreuil, Taxi Marco shuttle, transportation, charging station, electric vehicle, Tesla","t":"Auberge du Mont-Rigaud, 20, rue Bourget, Rigaud (7.3 km): 450-451-2202, aubergemontrigaud.com Travelodge, 50, rue Saint-Jean-Baptiste Ouest, Rigaud (10 km, 35 rooms): 450-451-4726 Holiday Inn Express, 33, boul. de la Cité-des-Jeunes Est, Vaudreuil (32 km, 134 rooms): 450-455-5522 Château Vaudreuil, 21700, route Transcanadienne, Vaudreuil-Dorion (34 km, 116 rooms): 450-455-0955 Taxi Marco shuttle: 450-764-3333 (advance booking only) Electric vehicles 4 charging stations on site, including 1 Tesla charger"},{"s":"Your suppliers","p":"To share with your suppliers","u":"your-suppliers.html#to-share-with-your-suppliers","k":"suppliers, arrival, setup, departure, 1 hour after","t":"Share this post with each of your suppliers. Arrival: tell your wedding coordinator each supplier's arrival time, so our team can welcome them. Equipment: your suppliers check and test their equipment in advance. Departure: they leave the hall no later than 1 hour after the end of the evening and pick up their equipment the next day, no later than 7:30 a.m. Complete list: give your wedding coordinator the names of all your suppliers. Some are not allowed on the premises because of past experiences."},{"s":"Your suppliers","p":"Cake and flowers","u":"your-suppliers.html#cake-and-flowers","k":"cake, flowers, florist, delivery","t":"The cake and flowers are delivered on the day, or as arranged in advance with your wedding coordinator. Floral arrangements arrive ready: the hall cannot be used to cut flowers or assemble arrangements, otherwise cleaning fees apply."},{"s":"Your suppliers","p":"DJ, musicians and photo booth","u":"your-suppliers.html#dj-musicians-and-photo-booth","k":"DJ, music, musicians, photo booth","t":"Your DJ or musicians work closely with the person in charge of your hall all evening, to synchronize meal service and entertainment. The team leader may adjust service timing as needed. The photo booth is set up in the location designated or approved by your wedding coordinator."},{"s":"Your suppliers","p":"Our favourite suppliers","u":"your-suppliers.html#our-favourite-suppliers","k":"suppliers, recommended, favourites","t":"Trusted partners we have seen at work here: officiants, music, flowers, cakes, photography, beauty, decor and more. Find their up-to-date contact details on our supplier page: Our favourite suppliers"},{"s":"The wedding day","p":"Who does what on the wedding day","u":"the-wedding-day.html#who-does-what-on-the-wedding-day","k":"wedding day, roles, banquet manager, trusted person","t":"Your banquet manager: on site from 2 p.m., she is your contact person at the Auberge and oversees the flow of the reception and the schedule in our spaces. Our service team: follows as closely as possible the flow set with you and your DJ (receiving line, dances, speeches). Your trusted person: transportation, outside suppliers, photos, transitions outside our facilities and unexpected situations. Introduce your trusted person to the banquet manager as soon as she arrives."},{"s":"The wedding day","p":"Your day, step by step","u":"the-wedding-day.html#your-day-step-by-step","k":"flow, schedule, ceremony, cocktail, reception","t":"From 8 a.m.: access to your reception hall for decorating. Getting ready: couple's room available from 1 p.m. at the latest; lunch in your room by pre-order; allow at least two hours to get dressed. Ceremony: the bride waits in her room until the wedding coordinator comes to get her. Cocktail: our team directs your guests to the planned space. Reception: place cards set on the tables by you or your trusted person; cake-cutting photos before the main course if the cake is served as dessert. 1 a.m.: end of the reception (until 3 a.m. with an extension, Phoenix and Pavillon only). The day after: breakfast for guests staying at the Auberge, pick-up of your belongings no later than 7:30 a.m. and settlement of the open tab, if any."},{"s":"The wedding day","p":"Breakfast the next morning","u":"the-wedding-day.html#breakfast-the-next-morning","k":"breakfast, next morning, overnight guests, billing, 8 a.m. to 10 a.m.","t":"Your guests staying at the Auberge start the day with breakfast, served from 8 a.m. to 10 a.m. Would guests staying elsewhere like to join you? Note how many in the \"La Grande Finale\" form, with the planned payment method: at your expense or billed to each guest."},{"s":"The wedding day","p":"Your wedding day kit","u":"the-wedding-day.html#your-wedding-day-kit","k":"kit, list, cake knife, rings, envelopes","t":"Entrust these items to a designated person: Cake knife and toasting glasses Guest book and card box Suppliers' payment and tip envelopes Wedding rings List of suppliers and their contact details Flow of the day and list of speeches"},{"s":"Special touches","p":"Our maple favours","u":"special-touches.html#our-maple-favours","k":"favours, maple, guest gifts, souvenir","t":"A sweet souvenir from our maple grove and the Sucrerie des Gallant, to offer your guests. Our maple syrup bottles come in four sizes: Medium maple leaf, 100 ml Large maple leaf, 250 ml Mini jug, 100 ml Jug, 250 ml Ask your wedding coordinator to place your order."},{"s":"Special touches","p":"Spa Gallant","u":"special-touches.html#spa-gallant","k":"spa, massage therapy, massage, treatment, relaxation","t":"The day before the wedding, treat yourself to a moment of relaxation: a massage therapy treatment at Spa Gallant. Reservation required for massage therapy treatments: arrange it with your wedding coordinator, no later than the final meeting."},{"s":"Special touches","p":"The outdoor fire pit","u":"special-touches.html#the-outdoor-fire-pit","k":"fire pit, campfire, outdoor, late evening, option, $75","t":"End the evening around the fire, under the stars: offer your guests an outdoor fire. $75, plus taxes and service charges Unlimited firewood You choose the time the fire is lit Indicate your choice and preferred time in the \"La Grande Finale\" form, on the \"Wine, bar and late evening\" page."},{"s":"Special touches","p":"The late-night buffet","u":"special-touches.html#the-late-night-buffet","k":"buffet, late night, poutine, pizza, platters","t":"To keep the fun going: see the late-night buffet in the \"Menu, bar and tasting\" section."},{"s":"Downloadable tools","p":"Planning timeline (Excel)","u":"downloadable-tools.html#planning-timeline-excel","k":"timeline, Excel, calendar, dates","t":"Enter your wedding date: all deadlines are calculated automatically and change colour as each step approaches. Planning timeline (Excel)"},{"s":"Downloadable tools","p":"Wedding budget (Excel)","u":"downloadable-tools.html#wedding-budget-excel","k":"budget, expenses, Excel","t":"Enter your maximum budget: the dashboard shows you at a glance whether you are within budget. Then enter, item by item, your estimates, actual costs, deposits and the status of each expense: totals, variances and the balance due are calculated automatically. Wedding budget (Excel)"},{"s":"Downloadable tools","p":"Floor plans of our reception halls","u":"downloadable-tools.html#floor-plans-of-our-reception-halls","k":"floor plans, PowerPoint, tables, scale","t":"Floor plans of Phoenix Hall, Vaudreuil-Soulanges Hall, Le Cellier and the Pavillon des Gallant, with scale table cut-outs and an editable PowerPoint to create your floor plan. Floor plans of our reception halls (ZIP)"},{"s":"Downloadable tools","p":"Place card guide and templates","u":"downloadable-tools.html#place-card-guide-and-templates","k":"place cards, guide, templates, symbols","t":"Our reference guide, with good examples and examples to avoid, and ready-to-fill templates that include our allergy symbols. Place card guide (PDF) Place card templates (ZIP)"},{"s":"Downloadable tools","p":"\"La Grande Finale\" form","u":"downloadable-tools.html#la-grande-finale-form","k":"Grande Finale, final meeting, form, count, meal choices, allergies, schedule","t":"Your final meeting form, one page per moment of the day: getting ready, ceremony, cocktail, reception, wine and bar, outdoor fire pit, late-night buffet, next-morning breakfast, meal choices, setup and suppliers. Fill it out on screen and send it to mariage@gallant.qc.ca one month before the wedding. \"La Grande Finale\" form (PDF)"},{"s":"Downloadable tools","p":"Nearby lodging and transportation","u":"downloadable-tools.html#nearby-lodging-and-transportation","k":"hotels, Rigaud, Vaudreuil, Taxi Marco shuttle, transportation, charging station, electric vehicle, Tesla","t":"See the sheet in the Accommodations section"}];
